== Notes ==
* Great Gideon can be instantly killed with {{p|Chaos Card}}. Doing so reveals a unique 1x2 {{r|Crawl Space}} beneath him, containing two locked chests, two items and a random key.
** This can be done at any time, even if he has already been defeated, as his deactivated body still remains after returning to the room.
** Defeating Great Gideon in this way plays a unique animation in which the Chaos Card gets lodged in his forehead before he explodes.
** Pressing on a {{E|Killswitch}} in the room similarly kills Great Gideon, and reveals the unique 1x2 {{r|Crawl Space}}. This also plays the unique animation of the {{p|Chaos Card}} in his head. Doing so is possible with {{i|D12}}
* Completing waves will not charge active items.
* {{i|Vanishing Twin}} will duplicate Great Gideon and increase the number of waves by 2. The waves themselves contain no extra enemies.
* Great Gideon can be fought outside the {{s|Mines}} or the {{s|Ashpit}} via using a {{p|IV - The Emperor?}} card in {{s|Downpour}} or {{s|Dross}}. If encountered outside his regular stages, he has preset waves consisting of {{e|Frowning Gaper}}s, {{e|Wall Creep}}s, {{e|Round Worm}}s, {{e|Gurgle}}s, and {{e|Sucker}}s.

== Trivia ==
* He is the boss version of {{e|Stone Grimace}}s, resembling a giant version with his left eye replaced by 7 holes arranged in a hexagonal pattern, and his left backside appears rougher with several protruding rocks.
** When performing his rock wave attack, he grows spikes resembling a {{e|Quake Grimace}}'s.
* Great Gideon's name likely comes from [[wikipedia:Gideon|Gideon]], an Old Testament prophet and military leader known for winning a decisive battle against an overwhelming Midianite army with only an army of 300 Israelites — explaining the large amount of enemies the boss spawns.
* The name Gideon is said to mean “hewer” which is an individual who works in a mine breaking stone.
* Great Gideon is one of the few bosses with a unique health bar, aside from {{e|Dogma}}.
* The {{r|Crawl Space}} that opens up when using {{p|Chaos Card}} on Gideon is titled "Gideon's Grave" in the game's code.
** According to artist NotYourSagittarius, this is a direct reference to ''Scott Pilgrim'', a series of graphic novels.

== Bugs ==
{{Bug|Spawning Great Gideon with the debug console will spawn him with a normal boss healthbar instead of a "waves" mechanic. When Great Gideon attempts to spawn a wave of enemies, the game crashes.}}
{{Bug|Dealing enough damage quickly enough (e.g. with {{i|Soy Milk}}) to the monsters Great Gideon creates can cause him to spawn the next wave before all enemies in the current one are dead.}}

